A||||5||Homicidal||Dome Lights will NOT turn OFF!  Help!||||11||
Z||000000||Homicidal||02-28-2001||03:38 AM||||Came home from dinner one night, found my domelight in my car on.<P>Thought maybe I left a door open.  Nope, all closed.<P>Thought I left the switch to "on" for the domelight.  Nope, off.<P>Nothing I did worked, so I pulled the fuse, and then pull the lightbulbs from the domelight and passenger car light.<P>Why is this happening?  Fuse is perfect, tried a new one also. <P>If it helps, it seemed to start after heavy rain (short?) and didn't happen too long before I came home or else the car would have been dead.<P>Any ideas?  <P>||||reg||11
Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||02-28-2001||05:58 AM||||Remove the door switches and check for shorts to ground. Should be easy to see.||||reg||1
Z||000002||rogergarrison||02-28-2001||06:06 AM||||there are 2 on/off switches for dome lites 1 is on the lite itself and the dash briteness switch under the head and park lite switch. Did you check both? Its ez to hit that when you turn your headlites off. Lisa did that the other day and didnt realize it.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Carrolles||02-28-2001||07:37 AM||||Also check the ctsy fuse.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Oreif||02-28-2001||09:44 AM||||Don't laugh, But check the cigar lighter fuse.<BR>GM vehicles use a "floating" ground system and I have seen the lighter fuse blow and cause the dome light to stay on.||||reg||1
Z||000005||ThatRickGuy||02-28-2001||10:15 AM||||ditto on the fuse thing, when I put in my new sterio, and turned on the dash lights I would blow a random fuse (but the sterio would still get power), turns out it had to do with the common ground and a floating voltage through the fuse box. altho 2 suggestions,<P>1. make sure it's not turned on by the dimmer switch<P>2. check the door switches for shorts.||||reg||1
